  "interpretation": "RDKit per-atom re-derivation of amine N-site structure agrees with the fixture for 2/2 target hardeners (True); both DETA and TETA are confirmed (per-atom, not asserted) to carry a pre-existing secondary amine N-H site (True). Validation gate: MC at r=1.0 reproduces the SIGNED analytic sol_wt_pct within tolerance on 6/6 checks. Across 18 (hardener x temperature-label x reactivity-ratio) combinations, the H2 direction rule holds in 18/18 cases. H2 is CORROBORATED for DETA/TETA (pre-existing secondary amine) across the full literature reactivity-ratio range and all 3 cure-temperature labels: the direction rule 'err amine-rich, never amine-starved' survives. AUDIT_ONLY; no candidate, product, objective, manifest edit, or promotion claim.",
