  "r_of_t_honest_scope": "No DETA/TETA-specific numeric r(T) function could be independently verified from accessible full text in this fire (Riccardi/Adabbo/Williams 1984 and Rozenberg 1986 are paywalled; WebFetch returned HTTP 402/403 on the DOI and ResearchGate pages attempted). Rather than fabricate an unverified curve, r is held at each literature-anchored value across all 3 temperature labels (an explicit, logged assumption grounded in Girard-Reydet et al. 1995's own finding, already in-tree via the parent receipt's does_not_close list, that r is approximately temperature-independent within their studied DSC range for a given diamine), and the full published r range (0.45-1.0) is swept at every temperature label so any real drift within that range is already bracketed. r_crit (below) gives the exact threshold a future fire with real DSC/full-text access can compare a measured r(T) curve against. Logged as does_not_close, not claimed as a measurement.",
